  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Looking at it, Corpse City is a city made from yellow clay. It is a huge mortal Gu House, like Dark Flow Giant City in Northern Plains Zombie Alliance’s branch.",
      "chapters": [
        1394
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_mortal_gu_house",
        "loc_dark_flow_giant_city",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "fac_zombie_alliance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fiend Mosquito tails Three Feather Boy hoping to find Corpse City of Zombie Alliance under translocation desert.",
      "chapters": [
        1393
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Western Desert Zombie Alliance’s true base had been an earth path blessed land. After Shadow Sect’s losses around sovereign immortal fetus Gu, that blessed land was discarded, resources were hidden in Corpse City, the mortal Gu House was moved under translocation desert, and a defensive Gu formation was activated. Corpse City sat inside the former blessed land arrangement before that move.",
      "chapters": [
        1394
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_western_desert",
        "fac_shadow_sect",
        "gu_sovereign_immortal_fetus_gu",
        "sys_gu_formation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan, as Shadow Sect’s leader, enters Corpse City easily and moves the entire city into his immortal aperture. Corpse City does not store Immortal Gu, but its defensive Gu formation uses Immortal Gu as cores.",
      "chapters": [
        1394
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "retrieval",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The formation uses rank seven Immortal Gu Fight and rank six earth path Immortal Gu Yellow Sand, plus mortal Gu, dense earth qi in the caves, and earth path dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        1394
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "formation-cores",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_yellow_sand_immortal_gu",
        "sys_mortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Yellow Sand looks like a ladybug with a round carapace and six yellow stars on it. Fang Yuan also finds Corpse City’s treasury of immortal materials inside the mortal Gu House, including cold moon divine bravery and phosphorescent wood.",
      "chapters": [
        1395
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "formation-cores",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
